<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="The nature and limits of China AI Hub content: informational only, not professional advice, AI-generated content disclosure, accuracy and timeliness limits, and how to request corrections."
  type="article"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: 2026-10-23</p>

    <h2>Scope of this disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      This disclaimer applies to <code>sinoaihub.com</code> and <code>data.sinoaihub.com</code>
      (together, "the site"), operated by the China AI Hub project. It explains the nature of the
      content, the limits of its accuracy and timeliness, our use of AI in producing the site, and
      how to report an error. It should be read together with the
      <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>, the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, and the
      <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      By using the site you acknowledge and accept the limitations described here. If you need
      verified, current, vendor-specific information before making a consequential decision, use the
      linked official source — that is the only place where binding terms, prices and capabilities
      are authoritatively stated.
    </p>

    <h2>Nature of the information</h2>
    <p>
      China AI Hub is an <strong>independent, informational and research platform</strong> about
      China's AI ecosystem. It is <strong>not an official source</strong>: it is not affiliated
      with, endorsed by, or operated by any AI vendor, and it does not speak for DeepSeek, Alibaba
      Cloud, ByteDance, Moonshot, MiniMax, Zhipu or any other company it describes. Information is
      compiled from public sources and presented for general reference; the authoritative source
      for any model, API or vendor is always that vendor's own documentation.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site publishes both <em>facts</em> and <em>analysis</em>, and keeps them distinct. Facts
      carry sources and verification dates; analysis is labeled "China AI Hub analysis" and is the
      project's own interpretation, not a claim about what any vendor has stated. You should treat
      analysis as opinion grounded in cited evidence, not as established fact.
    </p>

    <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is professional advice of any kind, and you should not rely on it as
      such. In particular:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Not investment or financial advice.</strong> The site is not a securities or
        financial publication. Statements about companies, pricing, markets or "positioning" are
        analysis, not recommendations to invest, buy, sell or hold any instrument or asset.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not procurement or deployment advice.</strong> Descriptions of models, APIs, licenses,
        regions and pricing are informational; a decision to adopt, buy, deploy or migrate to any
        model or vendor is yours alone. Verify against the vendor before committing production
        workloads, and consult your own legal and technical reviewers for licensing, data-residency
        and compliance questions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not legal, technical or security advice.</strong> The site does not provide legal
        opinions, security assessments, or compliance determinations. Licensing terms (for example,
        open-weight licenses and their commercial triggers) are summarized from public sources and
        are not a substitute for reading the license text itself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not an endorsement.</strong> Describing or comparing a model, company or API is not
        an endorsement of it, and the site's lack of coverage of a model is not a statement that the
        model is unsuitable.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI-generated content disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      The site discloses its use of AI-assisted tooling and labels the relevant content:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>AI-generated illustrations.</strong> Illustrations on entity pages are AI-generated
        (for example, using Seedream) and are labeled in their image credits. They are illustrative
        and contain no personal data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Automated verification tooling.</strong> The
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> documents that an automated agent re-fetches primary
        sources and compares extracted values against stored values during verification. This
        tooling supports data collection and verification; it does not author editorial content.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Editorial analysis.</strong> Text and analysis are produced and reviewed by the
        <a href="/authors/">SinoAI Hub Research Team</a>. Analysis is labeled "China AI Hub
        analysis" and is kept separate from observed, sourced fact.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      AI-generated output can be incomplete or wrong. Where it is used, it is reviewed against
      sources before publication; where a fact cannot be confirmed, the site marks it "Not publicly
      documented" rather than publishing a guess. The four claim labels used throughout the site —
      Official fact, Vendor-reported claim, Third-party evidence, and China AI Hub analysis — exist
      precisely so the reader can distinguish sourced fact from interpretation.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and timeliness</h2>
    <p>
      Facts on this site are sourced and date-stamped with a <code>last_verified</code> date, but
      the Chinese AI market changes quickly. Pricing, capabilities, licenses, regions and
      availability may become outdated between verification cycles. We update records when we detect
      changes, but we do <strong>not</strong> guarantee that the site is accurate, complete or
      current at the moment you read it. Figures should be verified against the linked official
      source before reliance.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a value is unknown, the site says so — it marks the value "Not publicly documented" or
      "Unknown" rather than guessing. The absence of a value is a statement about what is publicly
      documented, not a statement about what a model can or cannot do. Data is re-verified on a
      cadence described in the <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a> (weekly light checks, monthly
      full checks, and event-driven updates for major releases).
    </p>

    <h2>Specific disclaimers by content type</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Pricing.</strong> Prices are compiled from official pricing pages and are subject to
        change, currency differences, region differences, and peak/off-peak variation. They are
        informational estimates of listed prices, not quotations, and may not reflect your actual
        bill. Confirm current pricing and any discounts with the vendor.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Benchmarks.</strong> Benchmark scores are attributed to their reporting source and
        evaluation configuration. Vendor-reported scores reflect the vendor's own configuration and
        should not be compared directly against scores produced under different configurations.
        A score's absence for a model is not evidence of the model's capabilities.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Licenses.</strong> License summaries (including open-weight licenses and their
        commercial triggers) are simplified from public sources and are not legal advice; read the
        actual license text before redistributing or commercializing any model.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Availability and regions.</strong> Region and availability statements are accurate
        as of the recorded verification date and may change; confirm with the vendor before
        committing production workloads.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party information</h2>
    <p>
      The site reproduces and summarizes vendor claims and third-party data (including vendor-reported
      benchmark scores), always attributed to the reporting source. We do not independently
      re-verify a claim unless it is labeled as independently verified. Vendor-reported benchmark
      scores reflect the vendor's own evaluation configuration and should not be compared directly
      against scores produced under different configurations. Links to third-party sites are
      provided for reference and do not imply endorsement; we are not responsible for the content,
      accuracy or practices of any third-party site.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, completeness, merchantability, fitness
      for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be
      uninterrupted or error-free.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a free informational resource, not a paid service and not a provider of AI
      systems. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the China AI Hub project and its contributors
      are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or reliance on, the site —
      including reliance on model specifications, pricing, benchmarks, comparisons or analysis.
      Nothing in this disclaimer excludes liability that cannot be excluded under applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantee of availability</h2>
    <p>
      We do not warrant that the site will be available at all times or free of errors. The site is
      a static reference and may be modified, updated or temporarily unavailable without notice.
      The Data Hub (<code>data.sinoaihub.com</code>) is a companion property and may follow a
      separate update schedule.
    </p>

    <h2>Forward-looking and analytical statements</h2>
    <p>
      Some content discusses positioning, market structure and strategic implications (for example,
      a company's "structural role" in the ecosystem). These are the project's own analysis, labeled
      "China AI Hub analysis", and are not statements of fact, predictions, or guarantees of future
      performance. They should be read as interpretation grounded in the cited evidence, not as
      forecasts on which to base financial or business decisions.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party trademarks and content</h2>
    <p>
      Model names, company names, product names, benchmark names and logos referenced on the site
      are the trademarks or property of their respective owners and are used for identification only.
      Their use does not imply affiliation with, or endorsement by, those owners, and the site's
      independent analysis does not represent the views of any vendor. Any errors in summarizing
      third-party content are unintentional and will be corrected through the
      <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a> when reported.
    </p>

    <h2>No client or advisory relationship</h2>
    <p>
      Accessing the site does not create a client, advisory, fiduciary, or other professional
      relationship between you and the China AI Hub project. There is no paid advisory service, and
      no interaction with the site should be understood as the provision of bespoke advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe a fact, price, benchmark score or relationship on the site is wrong or
      outdated, report it through the <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a> — by email to
      <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a> or by opening an issue on the
      public project repository. Corrections are made through a recorded process; the current
      correction record is on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this disclaimer as the site's content or practices change. The "Last updated"
      date at the top reflects the current version. Because we maintain no mailing list, please
      review this page when you have concerns about the limits of the content.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this disclaimer or about the site's content: Martin.W —
      <a href="mailto:admin@sinoaihub.com">admin@sinoaihub.com</a>, or see the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Related pages: <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> ·
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> ·
      <a href="/about/">About</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How this disclaimer relates to the rest of the site</h2>
    <p>
      This page states the limits of the content; the other disclosure pages state how the content
      is produced and maintained. The <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> explains how data is
      collected and verified, the <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> define the
      quality gate, the <a href="/data-policy/">Data Policy</a> covers licensing and update
      cadence, and the <a href="/disclosure/">Funding Disclosure</a> explains the site's
      independence. The <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> are the binding rules governing use of
      the site; this disclaimer explains why you should not treat the content as advice or as a
      substitute for the vendor's own, current documentation.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
